WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.760
Look at this sleeper.

2
00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.440
Arms and legs completely still.

3
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.400
Now look at the brain: activity
close to waking levels,

4
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.780
eyes darting under closed lids.

5
00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:14.970
And a dream plays out: a
bus, suddenly a classroom,

6
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.250
then a beach.

7
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.740
So why does a busy brain,
in a body that can't move,

8
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.510
turn into a story?

9
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.960
In this mission, you'll see
what happens in REM sleep,

10
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.240
and why the body is paralysed.

11
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.350
You'll follow signals
firing up deep in the brain,

12
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.420
as your senses are shut
off from the outside world.

13
00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:37.720
And you'll find out where Hobson and
McCarley say the story comes from.

14
00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:42.190
Your mission: explain why
REM sleep turns into a story.
